{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZqTRafQGZR9XgBahiuW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` defines Shipment with statuses CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` has create, getById, list endpoints\n- ShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` provides save/findById/existsById\n- Error handling: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` defines ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- Error codes: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` enum defines codes like SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses: ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n- Error responses wrapped in envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": []}}`\n- Tests use @SpringBootTest with MockMvc and jsonPath assertions\n- Error code checking in tests via `jsonPath(\"$.error.code\").value(\"CODE_NAME\")`\n- Request/response payloads are Spring data classes\n\n**Affected files (cannot be avoided):**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — need new error code for invalid shipment status transition (409 on CANCELLED confirm)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — need to add `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint  \n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — need to add tests for all four scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if validation logic is wrong\n- Not implementing idempotency correctly (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED should succeed, not fail)\n- Using wrong HTTP status (409 for CANCELLED transition, not 400)\n- Missing the NOT_FOUND case (404)\n\n**Open questions:** None. Requirements are clear: CREATED→CONFIRMED (idempotent), CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED succeeds, CANCELLED→CONFIRMED is 409, unknown ID is 404.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment (HTTP 409).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Retrieves shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException if missing (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save, return updated shipment (200 OK)\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (200 OK) — making the operation idempotent\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - `test_confirms_a_created_shipment` — POST confirm on CREATED, expects 200 with status=CONFIRMED\n   - `test_idempotent_confirm_already_confirmed` — POST confirm twice on same shipment, second should still be 200\n   - `test_reject_confirm_cancelled_shipment` — POST confirm on CANCELLED (written directly to repo), expects 409 with error code\n   - `test_reject_confirm_unknown_shipment` — POST confirm on non-existent ID, expects 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could add a service layer between controller and repository, but the existing code has no service layer and keeping the same architecture is a constraint, so the logic stays in the controller like the create endpoint.\n- Could throw ValidationException instead of ConflictException for CANCELLED status, but the requirement says \"rejected with HTTP 409\" which is ConflictException's status, not 400.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | repository.save(updated) | 200 with shipment | return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | nothing | 200 with shipment | return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CANCELLED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | nothing | 409 ConflictException | throw ConflictException + GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Unknown ID | repository.findById(id) | nothing | 404 ResourceNotFoundException | throw ResourceNotFoundException + GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create shipment, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Confirm twice, verify both succeed and second returns same shipment\n- Test 3: Manually write CANCELLED shipment to repo, try to confirm, verify 409 with error code\n- Test 4: Try to confirm non-existent shipment, verify 404 with error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":16057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62ec3ac7-1cb2-445e-8c07-9e6f04ae31a5","uuid":"176af46d-de98-4eae-9aa9-eed50815c9e5","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:10:08.292Z","request_id":"req_011CfZqTREL37gVw8Kpsjpx4"}
